// A rope ladder tied on the lip of a 4 m cliff hangs down its face to the floor. The mole climbs it with W
// (2 m/s, slower than a wall climb), hangs still on it when it lets go of the keys (no sliding, unlike a
// wall), climbs on over the lip onto the top, and back at the foot a jump lets go of it.
map
##############################
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.................#
############.@...............#
##############################
##############################
##############################
end
give RopeLadder 1
place 2 -1 -10 RopeLadder         // beside the cliff: it ties on at the lip
expect 3 ladders == 1
hold 10-40 up                     // climb
expect 12 climbing == 1
expect 40 py < 21                 // going up...
expect 40 py > 15                 // ...at the ladder's pace (8 tiles/s)
expect 70 climbing == 1           // keys off: still on the ladder
expect 70 vy == 0                 // hanging still
hold 80-220 up left               // on up and over the lip
expect 240 py < 8                 // up on the cliff top
expect 240 grounded == 1
expect 240 px < 11                // standing on the cliff top
